From cf0e395c616c74ae7111769f8cbc2562c6594eb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:24:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] volumes: track and roll back acquired guest mounts

Keep ordinary filesystem mount ownership across container preparation,
agent errors and sandbox cleanup. Validate a reused mount before borrowing
it, retain failed cleanup for retry, and use the existing containerd mount
library for filesystem flags. Remove the superseded host-target wait path.

Exercise preparation and agent failure rollback, borrowed resources,
mount identity and optional loop-device readonly/no-format behavior.

Co-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
